      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>A pollution prevention inspection checks spill kits, oil storage, bunds and drains.</li><li>Oil storage above set volumes needs a bund under the Control of Pollution (Oil Storage) (England) Regulations 2001. Other nations have similar rules.</li><li>Know which drains are foul and which are surface water. Keep surface water drains clean.</li><li>A pollution incident means the Environment Agency, SEPA or NRW. An inspection costs far less.</li><li>Software does not stop a spill. The kit, the bund and a trained team do.</li></ul>"
    },
